# Rule - Definition of Done

Open the project files through `{workspace}/artifacts-map.md`. Join `{workspace}` and each stored path. Do not prefix `artifacts_root` again.

## Where the checklist lives

- A product backlog item (PBI) uses the Definition of Done section above the Product Backlog table in `product-backlog.md`.
- A sprint backlog item (SBI) uses the Definition of Done section above the first sprint table in `sprint-backlog.md`. A sprint may state a replacement checklist above its own tables. That checklist applies to that sprint only.
- An item acceptance line under a sprint adds to the checklist. It does not replace it.

## Before marking an item Done

1. Check every item in the checklist that applies.
2. Every acceptance criterion linked to the item has passed.
3. The user has confirmed the item is usable.
4. If any check is open, keep the status `WIP`.

A file on disk, a green local check, or met acceptance criteria alone is not Done.

An SBI can be `Done` while its parent PBI stays `ToDo` or `WIP` when the PBI checklist covers more than that SBI.

## Do not

- Mark an item Done without the user's confirmation.
- Remove or weaken a check to reach Done.
- Write Done into `status.md` for an item the backlog does not show as Done.
